  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FOREST DEPARTMENT-COMMUNITY PARTNERSHIP TO IMPROVE PROTECTION OF WESTERN HOOLOCK GIBBONS HOOLOCK IN JEYPORE, RF, INDIA -PHASE VIII</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to continue to support (1) the systematic field anti-poaching operations of three Roving Gibbon.Patrol Units (RGPU), each comprising of three community members and headed by a forest guard; (2) data reporting by RGPUs.and the maintenance of patrolling records by the Project Monitoring Assistant (PMA). The PMA will continue to compile the data.and produce monthly reports with maps, based upon which the field officer (Range Officer) will plan adaptive actions in.consultation with the RGPU; (3) compile, analyze and summarize all records from Phase I to Phase VIII in Year 3 of the project.to document total effort, challenges, outcomes, and lessons learned from this collaborative conservation model; and (4) a.systematic survey of hoolock gibbons using call and sightings in Year 2 of the project to estimate the gibbon population in.Jeypore.</narrative>
  </description>
